---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

// ⚠️  Plain-language terms written to be accurate about how the app behaves.
// NOT legal advice and NOT a reviewed contract — have a lawyer review before
// submitting to the App Store.
const updated = '5 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — QPushly"
  description="The terms under which you may use the QPushly Shopify app."
>
  <section class="phero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Terms of Service</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="upd font-mono text-xs text-muted mt-4">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec pt-4">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p>
        These terms cover your use of QPushly, a Shopify application that sends web
        push notifications from your store. By installing the app you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What the app does</h2>
      <p>
        QPushly lets you collect web push subscribers from your storefront and send
        them broadcast campaigns and event-triggered automations. Delivery uses the
        Web Push standard, which means it depends on the shopper's browser and on
        the push service operated by their browser vendor.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You are the controller of your shoppers' data. What you send, and to whom, is your decision.</li>
        <li>You will keep a privacy policy on your store that discloses your use of push notifications.</li>
        <li>You will not use the app to send unlawful, deceptive, harassing or misleading messages, and you will not impersonate anyone.</li>
        <li>You will not use the app to send notifications at a frequency intended to pressure or badger a shopper.</li>
        <li>You will comply with the marketing and consent laws that apply where your shoppers are.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Delivery is best-effort</h2>
      <p>
        We queue and sign your notifications and hand them to the shopper's push
        service. From that point delivery is outside our control: browsers throttle,
        revoke and expire subscriptions, devices go offline, and operating systems
        decide how and whether to display a notification. We do not guarantee that
        any particular notification is delivered, displayed, or seen.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the app available and will not deliberately take it down
        without notice, but we do not offer a service-level guarantee. Scheduled
        sends are processed on a recurring sweep, so a send may go out slightly after
        its scheduled time.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Fees and billing</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans are billed by Shopify through its billing system and appear on
        your Shopify invoice. Prices and plan contents are those shown by Shopify at
        the time you subscribe. You can upgrade, downgrade or cancel from the app's
        Billing page at any time; cancellation takes effect at the end of the
        current billing period, and we do not issue partial refunds for an unused
        part of a period. Uninstalling the app stops future charges.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Free plan</h2>
      <p>
        The free plan is offered as-is and may change. We will give notice in the app
        before reducing what the free plan includes.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your data remains yours. You can export your subscriber list at any time.
        Deletion is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>: tokens go
        on uninstall, everything else goes when Shopify sends the shop-redaction
        request that follows.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Suspension</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate access if the app is used in breach of these
        terms, in a way that harms shoppers, or in a way that threatens the stability
        or security of the service. Where circumstances allow, we will tell you first.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or
        consequential loss, including lost sales or lost profits, arising from use of
        the app or from any notification being delivered, not delivered, or delivered
        late. Our total liability is limited to the fees you paid us for the app in
        the twelve months before the claim.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced in the app, and
        the date at the top of this page will change. Continuing to use the app after
        a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
